# Implementation rules index

| Rule | Focus |
|------|--------|
| **project-context** | Always-on stack, layout, and task → rule router |
| **project-overview** | Pointer to `project-context` |
| **layer-structure** | Business / Data / UI / hosts and who may reference whom |
| **model-separation** | Domain types in Business, EF mapping in Data, no DTO stack |
| **migrations** | SQLite EF migrations via `dotnet ef`; safe changes for existing local databases |
| **localization-both-resx** | English and Serbian Latin keys, both catalogs in `UiLocalizer` |
| **testing** | Which test project owns domain, EF, UI strings, and multi-step flows |
| **concise-responses** | Short technical replies |
| **refactoring-and-rules** | Update rules when a refactor changes a convention |
| **issue-tracking** | Always-on: GitHub Issues plus one Project (Backlog → Ready → In Progress → Done) |
| **ticket-worktree** | Always-on: GitHub issue + sibling worktree before edits |
| **create-pr** | Explicit `@create-pr`: Bugbot, push, PR to `main`, remove the worktree |
| **review-pr** | Explicit `@review-pr`: standards review in `.cursor/skills/review-pr/` |

Skills: `github-ticket-flow` (`gh` commands for `issue-tracking`), `review-pr` (this review procedure).
